Subject: [PATCH 01286/11171] [conductor] In-process docs for ArcMemo v7:
 CROSS-GAME concept-library transfer (self-learning MANDATE; extends the
 exp4039 v6 within-game win): v6 compressed concepts into named abstractions
 and won WITHIN the milestone (59->18 actions). v7 tests the real
 self-learning claim -- does the library built from the 7 PRIOR solved games
 REDUCE the cost of solving a GENUINELY NEW 8th game (exp4049)? Seed exp4049's
 explore-first solver with the v6 library; measure action-count +
 induction-call reduction on the 8th game vs (a) a cold start and (b) v6's
 within-game-only memory. This is TRANSFER (across games), not replay (within
 one) -- the bar that distinguishes self-learning from caching.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
